1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,870
It's 1:30 in the morning.

2
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:06,730
You're in bed, and the classic late-night
thumb workout has officially begun.

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:08,430
You open the first video:

4
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:11,070
someone's holding an
injector pen and says,

5
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:14,890
"One shot, zero appetite,
I melted in half!"

6
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:18,490
One quick flick of the
thumb — bam — second video:

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,730
"I used this pen,
surprise, I got pregnant!"

8
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:23,290
Now look closely:

9
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:27,060
between those two videos,
there is only one thumb movement.

10
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:29,100
Zero point two seconds!

11
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:32,230
Watching that, your
brain immediately goes,

12
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,000
"Alright then, take the shot,

13
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:34,890
have a baby!"

14
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:39,920
But scientifically, connecting those dots
takes a little more work than swiping a

15
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:40,590
screen.

16
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:46,980
GLP-1 medications can indeed make an
indirect contribution to pregnancy chances

17
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,000
in some women;

18
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:50,940
but they are not direct
infertility treatments,

19
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:53,190
and they are not used during pregnancy.

20
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:54,980
I'm Doctor Senai Aksoy.

21
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,520
Today, let's look at the real connection
between these famous injections and

22
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:03,310
fertility, and what you need to
watch out for when planning a baby.

23
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:04,930
Let's start from the top:

24
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,310
what exactly is GLP-1?

25
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:09,820
It sounds like the newest
model of a hybrid car,

26
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:14,430
but it's actually a natural hormone
your body releases after a meal.

27
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:18,300
It plays a key role in fullness
and blood sugar regulation,

28
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:21,010
sending a very simple
message to the brain:

29
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,580
"We're good boss, we're full,

30
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:26,510
put the fork down slowly,
blood sugar is under control."

31
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:31,260
Medications like semaglutide and
liraglutide act like the official stunt

32
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:32,670
doubles for this hormone:

33
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,140
they mimic its effect.

34
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,380
Tirzepatide, on the other hand,

35
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,690
shows up with backup:

36
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:43,000
in addition to GLP-1, it also taps into
the effect of another hormone called

37
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,170
GIP.

38
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:48,930
In eligible people, they can help with
weight management and blood sugar control.

39
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:49,520
Great...

40
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:52,470
so how do we get from there to pregnancy?

41
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:56,780
A big part of the story happens
in Polycystic Ovary Syndrome,

42
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,930
or PCOS.

43
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:04,760
In some women with PCOS, insulin
resistance and irregular ovulation walk

44
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:06,030
hand in hand.

45
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:08,350
What is insulin resistance?

46
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:11,180
It's when insulin knocks
on the cell's door,

47
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:14,070
and from the inside, nobody answers:

48
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,240
the body doesn't respond
strongly enough to insulin.

49
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:20,890
When metabolic health and
weight management improve,

50
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:23,450
that internal chaos settles down.

51
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:26,220
In some women, periods
become more regular,

52
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:30,340
and the ovaries say, "Hey,
things finally calmed down in here,

53
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,410
how about we start ovulating again?"

54
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:37,350
Any boost to pregnancy chances —
at least in part — can come from there.

55
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:40,110
But watch out for the classic shortcut!

56
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:43,080
Not everyone with PCOS is overweight.

57
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,700
And not everyone who is overweight
has an ovulation problem.

58
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:50,240
So we cannot set up an
automatic equation that says,

59
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:53,930
"I have PCOS, therefore I need this shot."

60
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:56,250
So, are the studies promising?

61
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:58,030
Some of them, yes.

62
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:03,500
In women with PCOS, some research shows
improvements in cycle regularity and

63
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,430
spontaneous pregnancy rates.

64
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:07,380
But many of these studies are small,

65
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:10,550
and the medications and
add-on treatments vary.

66
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:15,300
And the fact that one single person on
social media got pregnant after taking the

67
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:19,210
drug does not directly prove
that egg quality improved.

68
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:21,170
That's not scientific evidence,

69
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,070
that's group chat science!

70
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:27,130
Besides, the results don't all
point in the same direction.

71
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:30,530
In a registry study published in 2026,

72
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:34,570
looking at women with infertility
and overweight or obesity,

73
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:39,790
semaglutide use was associated with
lower pregnancy and live birth rates.

74
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:42,020
Now don't jump to conclusions:

75
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:44,100
this is an observational study;

76
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:47,470
we cannot say the drug
directly caused that.

77
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:51,800
Factors like treatment timing and
intentionally delaying pregnancy may have

78
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:53,170
influenced the results.

79
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,860
We have to keep the endpoints separate:

80
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,450
getting regular periods, ovulating,

81
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,360
seeing a positive pregnancy test,

82
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:03,430
and having a live birth
are separate outcomes.

83
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:06,810
We cannot extrapolate these
findings to all women,

84
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:10,040
all GLP-1 medications, or to IVF.

85
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:15,980
We do not have strong, sufficient evidence
that GLP-1 drugs increase the chance of a

86
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,870
live birth in IVF.

87
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:24,030
The 2023 international PCOS guideline
makes this exact distinction:

88
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:29,510
these medications may be considered for
weight management in eligible individuals,

89
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:35,200
but using them specifically to improve
fertility outcomes in PCOS is restricted

90
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:36,750
to research settings.

91
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:41,010
Clinical use must be based on
a proper medical indication,

92
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,470
such as weight management or diabetes.

93
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:48,500
If pregnancy isn't happening in
PCOS because of a lack of ovulation,

94
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:51,620
and no other cause of
infertility is found,

95
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:56,930
the first-line ovulation treatment
recommended by guidelines is letrozole.

96
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:59,170
Now here is a crucial point.

97
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:01,600
Some patients calmly think, "Doctor,

98
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:04,320
I only get my period every three months,

99
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:05,580
I'm not gonna get pregnant."

100
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:08,000
Do not assume that!

101
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:11,770
Your body ovulates first,
and the period comes later.

102
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:16,370
When ovulation restarts, your ovaries
do not send you a text message:

103
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:19,410
pregnancy can happen
when you least expect it.

104
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:24,460
And we do not have sufficient human data
to say these medications are safe during

105
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:25,270
pregnancy.

106
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:30,400
That's why effective contraception is
essential both during treatment and during

107
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,530
the drug-specific washout period.

108
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:33,660
What is the timeline?

109
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:38,640
For semaglutide, stopping at least two
months before a planned pregnancy is

110
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:39,530
recommended.

111
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:43,270
For tirzepatide, that window
is at least one month.

112
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:46,660
Which medication you take,
the date of your last dose,

113
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:51,610
and when to start trying to conceive must
be clarified with the prescribing doctor.

114
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:53,850
Especially if you have diabetes,

115
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:58,090
pregnancy-safe blood sugar treatment
must also be planned in advance.

116
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:00,280
For those taking tirzepatide,

117
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,620
there is another very important detail.

118
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:06,090
Especially in people with
overweight or obesity,

119
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:09,490
the effectiveness of birth
control pills may decrease.

120
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,950
Because the drug changes how
fast the stomach empties,

121
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:14,890
absorption of the pill can drop.

122
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:20,010
So for four weeks after starting and
for four weeks after each dose increase,

123
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:23,840
using an additional barrier method
like a condom alongside the pill,

124
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:26,960
or switching to a non-oral
contraceptive method,

125
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:27,960
is recommended.

126
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:33,630
Keep in mind, this warning is not
identical across all GLP-1 drugs.

127
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:37,840
"Wait, Doctor — what if the pregnancy
test turns positive while I'm on the

128
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:38,650
medication?"

129
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:43,590
Contact your prescribing doctor
and your OB-GYN immediately;

130
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:47,230
these medications are not
continued during pregnancy.

131
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:52,310
Being exposed to the medication does
not mean the baby is definitely harmed.

132
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:55,780
Available human data are
reassuring in some respects,

133
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:59,310
though not strong enough
to confirm complete safety.

134
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:02,460
Your doctors will evaluate
which drug was used,

135
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:05,970
the dose, and at what stage
of pregnancy it was taken.

136
00:07:06,140 --> 00:07:10,810
If you have diabetes, alternative
treatment is started without delay.

137
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:14,930
Before IVF, your age, ovarian reserve,

138
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:19,980
the cause of infertility, and the impact
of waiting on your fertility must all be

139
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,990
weighed together.

140
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:22,420
Telling everyone at the door,

141
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:26,830
"Go lose weight first, then
we'll do treatment" is not right.

142
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:30,230
For some people, metabolic
preparation makes sense;

143
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:34,250
for others, delaying for a long
time may not be appropriate.

144
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:38,620
Your weight is not a grade on a report
card that decides whether you deserve

145
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:39,430
treatment.

146
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:41,810
And if an egg retrieval is planned,

147
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:47,050
make sure you tell your IVF team and your
anesthesiologist about your medication.

148
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:50,450
Never think, "Oh, it's
just my weight-loss pen,

149
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:51,520
no need to mention it."

150
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:55,080
These medications slow
down stomach emptying.

151
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:57,280
Even if you've fasted for eight hours,

152
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:59,040
your stomach might not be empty,

153
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:02,980
and that matters a lot during
sedation or anesthesia.

154
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:07,880
The washout plan for pregnancy and the
pre-procedure anesthesia plan are not the

155
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:08,710
same thing:

156
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:11,530
let your team build your specific plan.

157
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:13,950
And then, there are the men!

158
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:17,460
Gentlemen, don't sit on the edge of
the couch watching this and saying,

159
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:20,080
"See honey, the doctor is talking to you."

160
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:25,600
In men with obesity, lifestyle changes
like nutrition and exercise can improve

161
00:08:25,620 --> 00:08:27,310
certain sperm parameters.

162
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:31,080
There is research on GLP-1
medications in men too,

163
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:33,170
but the evidence remains limited.

164
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:38,250
Today, we cannot present these drugs as
a proven treatment for male infertility.

165
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:40,800
Side effects like nausea, vomiting,

166
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:43,270
and gut issues can also happen.

167
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:46,540
And weight regain can occur
after stopping the medication.

168
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:49,730
That's why nutrition, physical activity,

169
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:54,770
metabolic follow-up, and the transition to
pregnancy should all be planned together.

170
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:58,220
Folks, clarify these three
things with your doctor:

171
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,340
One.

172
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:01,800
Why do I medically need this medication?

173
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:02,960
Two.

174
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:05,460
When should I stop it
before trying to conceive,

175
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:08,440
and how should I use
contraception during that time?

176
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,520
Three.

177
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:12,620
How does this affect the timeline
of my fertility treatment?

178
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:18,420
This content is for informational purposes
and does not replace an individual medical

179
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,080
evaluation.
